ties Catering & Food Services Lodging Options Conferences & Meetings Retreats & Camps Weddings & Banquets News & Media News & Media News Brand Toolkit Media Relations Info For: Info For: Current Students Parents & Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni Home > Jobs at Manchester University Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid » Undergraduate Admissions First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Veterans Early College Experience Admitted Students Commit Graduate Admissions International Student Admissions Articulations & Course Equivalencies Manchester University Tuition and Fees Student Financial Services Financial Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans Federal Aid Work Study Graduate Financial Aid Award Notification Glossary FAFSA Verification Life After Manchester Apply Visit Our Campus Campus Map Food & Lodging Request More Info Experience Manchester for Yourself Schedule Your Visit Academics Academics » Programs & Degrees Online Degrees Undergraduate Studies Core Curriculum Honors Program Experiential Learning Degree in 3 Fast Track Academic Enrichment Honors & Awards Graduate Studies Plus Programs Colleges On-Demand Training Manchester University Fort Wayne Faculty & Staff Directory Student Success Academic Support Academic Calendar Graduation Career & Professional Development Registrar What programs does Manchester offer? Find your program Student Life Student Life » Housing & Dining East Hall East Street Apartments Garver Hall Helman Hall Oakwood Hall New Student Information Consolidation Spiritual Life Fellowship & Ministry Groups Spartan Stories Events Life at Manchester Campus Life Clubs & Activities Athletics & Recreation Campus Safety Manchester Together NxtGen Program on Campus Campus Support Health & Well-being Esports Join us Mondays at 11 a.m. VIA Schedule Athletics About About » MU at a Glance Mission & Values Our History Leadership Assessment & Accreditation Institutional Effectiveness Accreditation Assessment Faculty & Staff Directory Conference Services North Manchester Campus Facilities Fort Wayne Campus Facilities Catering & Food Services Lodging Options Conferences & Meetings Retreats & Camps Weddings & Banquets News & Media News Brand Toolkit Media Relations Bring the whole family Homecoming a M Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid » Undergraduate Admissions First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Veterans Early College Experience Admitted Students Commit Graduate Admissions International Student Admissions Articulations & Course Equivalencies Manchester University Tuition and Fees Student Financial Services Financial Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans Federal Aid Work Study Graduate Financial Aid Award Notification Glossary FAFSA Verification Life After Manchester Apply Visit Our Campus Campus Map Food & Lodging Request More Info Experience Manchester for Yourself Schedule Your Visit Academics Academics » Programs & Degrees Online Degrees Undergraduate Studies Core Curriculum Honors Program Experiential Learning Degree in 3 Fast Track Academic Enrichment Honors & Awards Graduate Studies Plus Programs Colleges On-Demand Training Manchester University Fort Wayne Faculty & Staff Directory Student Success Academic Support Academic Calendar Graduation Career & Professional Development Registrar What programs does Manchester offer? Find your program Student Life Student Life » Housing & Dining East Hall East Street Apartments Garver Hall Helman Hall Oakwood Hall New Student Information Consolidation Spiritual Life Fellowship & Ministry Groups Spartan Stories Events Life at Manchester Campus Life Clubs & Activities Athletics & Recreation Campus Safety Manchester Together NxtGen Program on Campus Campus Support Health & Well-being Esports Join us Mondays at 11 a.m. VIA Schedule Athletics About About » MU at a Glance Mission & Values Our History Leadership Assessment & Accreditation Institutional Effectiveness Accreditation Assessment Faculty & Staff Directory Conference Services North Manchester Campus Facilities Fort Wayne Campus Facilities Catering & Food Services Lodging Options Conferences & Meetings Retreats & Camps Weddings & Banquets News & Media News Brand Toolkit Media Relations Bring the whole family Homecoming Info for: Future Spartans Current Students Parents & Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni Home > Jobs at Manchester University Give Request Info Visit Apply Jobs at Manchester University Jobs at Manchester University? Why Work at MU? Your Value as an Employee Explore jobs at Manchester University, where we value the infinite worth of every individual and graduate students of ability and conviction who are equipped to impact lives and change the world. As a part of MU’s team, you will find rewarding employment opportunities and jobs to invest in the lives of students and be connected to a community of people who care about you personally. Take a moment and hear why Garrett and Sarah work at Manchester. Meet Garrett Schieferstein Meet Sarah Emerich Faculty & Staff Jobs Visit Campus Student Jobs Hiring Process Step 1 | Apply for the position You’ve successfully submitted your application via ADP and received a confirmation email. The next step in the process is for your application to be reviewed by the hiring supervisor and/or search committee. Successful candidates will be contacted for an interview. Step 2 | Interviews A Manchester representative will contact you to schedule an initial interview. These are often conducted via telephone or video calls. This is an opportunity to learn more about the position and University, as well as expound on your strengths and qualifications. Tell us why you are the best candidate for the job! Second interviews are generally held on campus. The format will vary based on the type of position. Once the applicant pool has been narrowed down to the top candidates, the hiring manager will conduct reference checks. Step 3 | Offer of employment Human Resources will make a verbal offer of employment to the selected candidate. After any negotiations have been made and approved, an official, written offer of employment is then emailed to the candidate. This will include confirmation of position title, start date, compensation, and any other pertinent information. All other candidates who were not selected will receive a declination notification. Step 4 | New Hire Paperwork The new employee will return their signed offer letter, a personal data form, and provide consent for background check screening. HR will enter the employee into the HRIS and process the background check. Next, the employee will receive a notification to complete onboarding tasks via ADP. Step 5 | You’re Hired! Welcome to the team! The first day of employment will be spent in orientation on our North Manchester campus. The new employee will receive details regarding what to bring and expect prior to the first day. Meet the Human Resources Staff Hanna Fisher Talent Acquisition Coordinator hmfisher@manchester.edu 260-982-5713 READ MORE Heather Hess Director of Human Resources HNHess@manchester.edu 260-982-5288 READ MORE Jadon Boyce Human Resource Generalist 260-982-5559 READ MORE Employee Benefits Overview Contact Us: For more information, contact the Office of Human Resources at hr@manchester.edu or call 260-982-5191 . Employee Handbook ADP Portal ADP Portal links: MU Employees Previous MU Employees Domestic Partner Benefits Manchester University provides certain benefits to its employees’ domestic partners and their children who meet eligibility criteria. Please consult the Employee Handbook for details. Employee Assistance Program All full-time and part-time employees and their immediate family members are eligible to participate in the employee assistance program (EAP) provided through the Bowen Center. Each family member is eligible to receive five prepaid sessions of outpatient counseling per year at one of the 11 Bowen Center locations. The service is completely private and confidential. The University pays 100 percent of the premium. In addition, all full-time and part-time employees and their immediate family members are eligible to participate in the employee assistance program (EAP) provided through Symetra. Each family is eligible to receive three prepaid sessions of outpatient counseling per year with a Symetra provider. The service is completely private and confidential. The University pays 100 percent of the premium. Golf Membership Opportunity All employees are eligible for a discounted golf membership at the Sycamore Golf Club. Family members may be added for a fee. Health Insurance Health Insurance We want to ensure that you have the ability to enroll and choose a medical plan(s) that best meet the needs of your family. To do this, we will connect you with Remodel Health who will help you. We provide a monthly wage increase to employees that may be used for the purchase of medical plans. You are encouraged to use the wage increase to purchase medical plans, but you are not required to do so. Remodel Health is an employer provided service. The Remodel Health platform allows you to choose an individual health plan or program specific to your individual needs. Health Savings Account (HSA) Persons enrolled in a high deductible health plan are eligible to open a health savings account (HSA) and will receive semi-annual employer contributions. Flexible Spending Accounts (IRS Section 125) Voluntary flexible spending accounts allow employees to set aside pre-tax income dollars to pay for various medical, dental and dependent care expenses. To participate, new hires MUST enroll within 30 days of employment or at the next open enrollment period (typically November of each year). Life Insurance and Accidental Death and Dismemberment The University provides basic life and ADD insurance coverage for all employees. Long-term Disability Insurance (LTD) The University provides long-term disability insurance benefits to full-time employees under the age of 65. The plan will provide disabled employees 60 percent of their monthly salary not to exceed $10,000 per month. The University pays 100 percent of the premium, however, employees will be taxed on the premium. Other Benefits Financial support for professional meetings Discounted meals at Sodexo in Haist Commons Complimentary tickets to Public Program Series, athletic events and more No-cost parking on campus with employee parking permit Direct deposit of payroll check Paid Time Off Paid Time Off Policy Paid time off (PTO) is awarded on January 1. Employees hired mid-year will receive a pro-rated amount as determined by their hire dates. 0-9 years of service 0-9 years of service 10+ years of service 10+ years of service Full-time, 12-month staff and faculty 224.00 28 264.00 33 Full-time, 10-month staff 186.67 23 224.00 28 Full-time, 9-month staff 168.00 21 204.00 25.5 Part-time staff 132.24 16 132.24 16 9- and 10-month faculty 60.00 7.5 60.00 7.5 Nine- and 10-month faculty members receive paid time off automatically during periods when classes are not in session. Faculty will be expected to use PTO for their own or a dependent’s illness, doctor appointments or other “sick” related events. Paid Holidays Manchester University provides regular full-time employees 9 paid holidays annually. Additionally, each full-time staff member and 12-month faculty members may earn one floating wellness holiday after participating in pre-approved, wellness-related activities. Official Manchester University holidays are as follows: New Year’s Day Martin Luther King Jr. Day Good Friday Memorial Day Independence Day Thanksgiving and the day after Christmas Holiday- Christmas Eve through New Year’s Eve Wellness Day (after earning and with supervisor’s approval) Eligibility Employees are eligible immediately for holiday pay upon hire. Part-time staff who work a minimum of 1,040 hours per year (average 20 hours per week) are eligible for holiday pay on a prorated basis. Floating holidays are also prorated. PERC Membership All employees receive a no-charge family membership to the Physical Education and Recreation Center (PERC), which features racquetball, exercise and weight room, arena, etc. Retirement Plan Full-time employees are eligible to participate in the University’s retirement program through TIAA following a one-year waiting period. The University contributes a percentage of annual gross earnings. Employees choose investment vehicles. University contributions are fully vested immediately. Short-term Disability Coverage (STD) The University provides STD coverage to all full-time employees, following six months of continuous service. The plan will provide disabled employees 60 percent of their salary up to $5,000 for up to 26 weeks per incident. Benefits begin following the seventh day of disability. Supplemental Retirement Account Employees may establish their own supplemental retirement account (SRA). Voluntary employee contributions may be made on a tax-deferred basis or post-tax in a ROTH account. Employees can begin participation the first of the month following the date of hire. Tuition Remission Full-time employees, their spouses, and children under age 24 are eligible for f ull tuition remission at the beginning of the semester following the start of full-time work by the employee, providing other qualifying criteria have been satisfied. Part-time, 12-month employees (scheduled for between 20-30 hours per week), their spouses, and children under age 24 are eligible for one-half tuition remission at the beginning of the semester following the start of part-time work by the employee, providing other qualifying criteria have been satisfied. Employees who are scheduled to work less than 20 hours per week are not eligible for this benefit. Please see the Employee Handbook for details. Vision Plan Basic vision coverage is provided to all benefits-eligible employees and their eligible dependents, with the premium covered by MU. Voluntary Group Dental Plan The University makes available voluntary group dental insurance. Voluntary Group Term Life Insurance Employees may choose to purchase additional group term life insurance coverage for themselves and their dependents, if eligible. Title IX Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow NORTH MANCHESTER 604 E College Ave. PO Box 365 North Manchester, IN 46962 260-982-5000 FORT WAYNE 10627 Diebold Rd. Fort Wayne, IN 46845 260-470-2700 Request Info Visit Give Apply Refer a student Jobs at Manchester University Book an Event Canvas News Bookstore Events Library Quick Links Recruit Me FERPA Title IX Privacy Policy Nondiscriminatory Policy Annual Security Reports Hazing Policy/Hazing Transparency Report ©2026 Manchester University"
    }
